-------------------------------------------------------------
--- DEFAULT GEOMETRY — PRIMARY APPLICATION WINDOWS ONLY   ---
-------------------------------------------------------------
-- The default size/centre must not touch dialogs, menus, dropdowns or tooltips.
-- Those are separate toplevels, so a plain `class = ".*"` size rule stretches
-- them to the full 2540x1300 instead of leaving them at their natural size next
-- to whatever opened them.
--
-- match.float is the discriminator. By the time window rules are evaluated,
-- CHyprXWaylandManager::shouldBeFloated() has already run and set the floating
-- state, and it floats anything the client presents as transient:
--   X11     - _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_{DIALOG,MENU,DROPDOWN_MENU,POPUP_MENU,TOOLTIP,
--             TOOLBAR,UTILITY,SPLASH,DOCK}, _KDE_NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_OVERRIDE,
--             modal windows, transients, override-redirect windows, anything
--             with a parent, and fixed-size windows (min hints == max hints)
--   Wayland - any xdg_toplevel with a parent, or one with a fixed size
--
-- `float = true` above does not interfere: it is staged as static_.floating and
-- only committed after the rule pass, so it never feeds back into this match.
--
-- So match.float = false means "the client did not ask to be transient", i.e. a
-- primary application window. Everything else keeps the geometry it requested.
-- This is toolkit-agnostic (GTK, Qt, Electron, Java, wine) — no per-app rules.
hl.window_rule({
    name  = "default-size-primary-only",
    match = { class = ".*", float = false },

    size   = "2540 1300",
    center = true,
})

-------------------------------------------------------------
--- PER-APP SIZES (these intentionally win over the above) --
